# Wave W17-Z (Lake Insight): calm turf — frozen-shore snow turf, honest-white flecks: the brightest snow ground in Borea, a green-white calm carrying faint cool flecks and the odd sparkle, the kept shore of the lake of knowledge (design: the ice keeps the surface; the warden’s tracks cross the preserved icepool — drawn on that surface’s own art register, the cells never moving). Lake Insight’s own snow ground — split from its twin Lake Gallant by season entire (the frozen lake vs the bright open water) and from Route 217’s white turf behind it by temperature: lake-calm green-white vs bench blue-white. Pale, cold, unbroken — the winter form of the ground law.
